From b6674f5447ba008872d8f3f97c9ac2d45ad61c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hleb Shauchenka <me@marleb.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:39:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: register hwmon thermal zones

The Realtek PHY hwmon device exposes the PHY temperature, but its
channel info lacks HWMON_C_REGISTER_TZ, so the hwmon core does not
register the sensor with the thermal framework and device-tree
thermal zones that reference the PHY cannot bind. The RTL8261N
cooling maps of the Zyxel XGS1250-12 depend on it.

Mainline declined it: no mainline board describes these PHYs in its
device tree, and the RTL8261N support that needs it is OpenWrt's
pending 742. Carry it until RTL8261N support reaches mainline.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/ed20a09c-e275-4124-90b7-8b1ada9fbf91@lunn.ch/
Signed-off-by: Hleb Shauchenka <me@marleb.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_hwmon.c
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ static const struct hwmon_ops rtl822x_hw
 };
 
 static const struct hwmon_channel_info * const rtl822x_hwmon_info[] = {
+	HWMON_CHANNEL_INFO(chip, HWMON_C_REGISTER_TZ),
 	HWMON_CHANNEL_INFO(temp, HWMON_T_INPUT | HWMON_T_MAX),
 	NULL
 };
